      "exact_reserve_text": "Healthcare: Dale has written institutional healthcare professional liability business since 2016. We reviewed the reserves during 4Q24 on the US portfolio in response to experiencing an increase in severe claims, above expectations, during the year, but most pronounced in the 4th quarter. For context, during 2024 the actual incurred development was GBP 28.3m against expected development of GBP 8.4m. We have increased reserves on all years. The 2022 and prior gross reserves were increased by GBP 21.3m, partially offset by increased reinsurance recoveries of GBP 4.7m. Aviation War: During 4Q24 a number of claims have been agreed for settlement, but not yet, settled, on an ex-gratia basis against policies written under an aviation war consortium. Dale has a small following line participation. The increase in reserve is GBP 12.8m gross, GBP 5.1m net of reinsurance. US General Liability: We continue to see adverse development of claims predominantly in respect of two contracts and have strengthened gross (and net) reserves by GBP 5.4m for the 2022 and prior years.",
